            <ArticleTitle>[Pathogenesis of acute ulcers of the digestive tract in post- operative suppurative-septic complications].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In studying the pathogenesis of acute gastric and duodenal ulcers arising in operated patients against the background of purulent-septic complications, the specific signs distinguishing them from stress-ulcers, which develop in response to surgical aggression, were revealed. They are: the absence of inflammatory reaction in the gastric mucosa, its ischemia, hypo- and achlorhydria with reduction in the proteolytic activity of gastric juice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
